hud-recomp.patch - what the new HUD (tools/godot/project/hud, docs/issues/native-hud.md) needs changed in files
that are other agents'.  The text before the first "---" line is notes; `patch -p1 --dry-run < tools/godot/hud-recomp.patch`
from the workspace root applies the two hunks below (made against tools/recomp and tools/godot as they stood on
2026-10-13 15:25 (drivers.cpp) and 15:50 (rtag.cpp); built and run in local/godot-hud/root on the 15:25 state).

1. MUSIC VOLUME (the two hunks below; Ran).
   The sound core mixes music apart from the rest: the stream driver's stream 2 is the music (speech is streams 0 and
   1, effects are voices of their own).  tools/recomp/sound/drivers.cpp gets a host gain for stream 2 only, applied
   where the driver's timer writes a stream's voice volume; tools/godot/lib/rtag.cpp hands it out as
   rtag_set_option("music_volume", "0..1").  The music director (project/hud/music/music.gd) asks for it through
   RtaMachine.set_option and, when the library answers "no such option", ducks the whole game mix by 14 dB instead.
   Ran with only stream 2 rendered (--opt sound-solo=stream2), first level, level of the game's sound on a bus of its
   own: 1.0 -> mean -24.5 dB, 0.0 -> silence after the driver's own fade, 0.25 -> mean -32.9 dB.  With the whole mix
   (the narrator speaking over the music) the same three settings gave -21, -23, -24 dB: speech and effects stay.

2. THE GAME'S OWN HUD, SECOND GROUP (asked for; NOT in this patch: it changes the translation).
   rtag_set_option("game_hud", "off") hides the five wrapped HUD draws.  Three things of the game's HUD are drawn by
   two functions that are not wrapped and still show: the boss meter and the one-line message (both in
   hud_drawBossMeter 0x1d93b0), and the interaction prompt box (hud_drawPromptBox 0x1d99f0, also used by the spell
   selector).  Wanted: both addresses in tools/recomp/hle.txt, wrapped in app/gfx_rt.cpp under a mark of their own that
   keeps the default (centred) layout but can be left out, and a second option the HUD already asks for:
       rtag_set_option("game_hud_text", "off")
   While that option is refused the HUD does not draw its own message and prompt over the game's (mode "both" does,
   for comparing), keeps its own boss bar at the top, and moves its quick slots above the game's meter while a boss
   is up.  In a view that leaves the player's model out (first person) the game's prompt is not drawn at all
   (Player_draw draws it): there the HUD always draws its own.

3. THE VIEW OF A FRAME IN THE OVERHEAD VIEW (asked for; a few lines in tools/godot/lib/rtag.cpp, view_drawn).
   rtag_frame.view has valid = 1 but eye / forward / right / up all zero while the overhead view is selected (no view
   code runs then).  The HUD falls back to the camera read from memory for that case (gamestate.cpp).  Better: fill
   the game's own camera of that draw pass (fpview::View.game_eye / game_forward / game_up / game_right, game_fov), so
   that every frame carries the camera it was drawn with.

4. WHAT THE CONTROLS SIDE KNOWS (asked for; tools/godot/lib/rtag.h + extension/src/rta_machine.cpp).
   fpcontrols::hud() (tools/recomp/app/fpcontrols.h) lives on the game's thread inside the library.  The HUD looks for
       RtaMachine.get_controls_hud() -> Dictionary
   with the fields of fpcontrols::Hud under their own names: reticle, ranged, look, behind, hits_taken,
   last_hit_bearing, melee / shot / locked as {valid, object, x, y, z, distance, bearing, hp, hp_max}, threats as an
   Array of {object, x, y, z, distance, bearing, targets_me, attacking, in_view}.  Used when there (world.gd _aim,
   threat.gd); without it the HUD derives the same from the creatures' own targets and places.

5. ALREADY MERGED by the Godot agent (nothing to do): GDREGISTER_CLASS(RtaGameState) in extension/src/register.cpp
   behind RTA_GODOT_HAVE_GAMESTATE, and the CMake lines that name tools/recomp/app for gamestate.h.

6. THE ONE LINE IN THE HOST (tools/godot/project/main.gd, in _ready after `add_child(view)`):
       add_child(load("res://hud/hud.tscn").instantiate())        # the new HUD (tools/godot/project/hud)

